  "created": "2019-08-18T01:34:40.121Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Version: 2019.2.5\n\n\nDescription of the bug: If the user has the 3Dconnexion drivers installed, upon logging in to VRChat in VR mode they will begin sliding forward and to the left and they will be unable to open the menu. Pressing the analog stick can temporarily stop the sliding, but as soon as the stick is released the user is sliding again.\n\nIt seems like because the device is not producing values VRChat is deciding that the analog input is stuck at -1,-1 instead of just ignoring it. Other software does not seem to have any problem. Other input devices may cause similar issues.\n\nUsing device manager to disable the 3Dconnexion KMJ Emulator device before starting VRChat seems to avoid the issue, but probably will break functionality provided by the 3Dconnexion driver until it is reenabled.\n\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?): Install the 3Dconnexion SpaceMouse driver and then start VRChat in VR mode.\n\n\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):",
